.TH 3DMOUSECTL 1 2026-11-10 "3dmouse-linux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
3dmousectl \- control and diagnose 3DMouse Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B 3dmousectl
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Broker, agent and the active profile.
.TP
.BR "devices list" ", " "devices inspect " [\fIUSB_ID\fR]
Detected devices. For each: descriptor, nodes, permissions and the registry entry.
.TP
.BR monitor " [\-\-duration 10s]"
Live axes and buttons.
.TP
.BR "profile list" | show | activate " ID [\-\-persist]" | auto | export | import | delete | backup | reset\-presets
Manage profiles.
.B import
is a dry run unless
.B \-\-apply
is given.
.TP
.BR "settings get" ", " "settings set " "KEY VALUE"
.TP
.BR calibrate " [\-\-duration 3s] [\-\-apply]"
Measure the neutral offset. Keep your hands off the device while it runs.
.TP
.BR test\-action " JSON [\-\-phase press|release]"
Run one action, for example
.BR '{"type":"key","keys":"ctrl+z"}' .
With
.BR "\-\-phase press" ,
a holdable action stays down until a matching
.BR "\-\-phase release" ;
this opens and closes a radial menu without a device.
.TP
.B diagnostics check
Checks udev permissions, services, competing daemons, the desktop and uinput.
The exit status is non-zero when any check fails.
.TP
.BR "diagnostics record" " [\-\-duration 10s] [\-\-redact] [\-\-output FILE]"
.TP
.BI "diagnostics replay " FILE
Runs a recording through the input pipeline.
.TP
.BR support\-bundle " [\-\-output FILE]"
A redacted support bundle. Serial numbers, window titles and key activity are never included.
.TP
.B service health
.TP
.B version
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on any failure (including usage errors).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR 3dmoused (8),
.BR 3dmouse-agent (1),
.BR 3dmouse-config (1)
